---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import StatusBadge from "../components/StatusBadge.astro";
import Disclaimer from "../components/Disclaimer.astro";
import { SITE, href } from "../site.config";
---

<BaseLayout title="Home">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Healthy hives, sharper eyes.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A photo check that helps beekeepers spot three honeybee diseases early, built from a
        final-year project at Namal University. It supports inspection. It never replaces it.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn" href={href("/detector")}>See how the detector works</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={href("/project")}>Read the project</a>
      </div>
      <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        {SITE.name}. The detector interface is built, and the converted models passed parity
        testing, but they are not published yet, so no analysis runs yet.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container">
    <section aria-label="Status">
      <h2 class="visually-hidden">Status</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Live detector</h3>
          <p><StatusBadge kind="pending" label="Live demo coming soon" /></p>
          <p>
            The detector interface, queue, history, and exports are built. The converted models
            passed parity testing but are not published yet, so the detector shows a coming-soon
            state and runs no analysis.
          </p>
          <p><a href={href("/detector")}>Open the detector</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Research paper</h3>
          <p><StatusBadge kind="pending" label="Under review" /></p>
          <p>
            The paper is under review. No title, abstract, or figures are published here until the
            team confirms what may be shared.
          </p>
          <p><a href={href("/research")}>Research summary</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Team statements</h3>
          <p>
            <StatusBadge kind="pending" label="Certificate to be added" />
            <StatusBadge kind="pending" label="Photos to be added" />
          </p>
          <p>
            Awards and field-work claims are statements by the project team, never verified
            facts. Certificates and photos are still to be added.
          </p>
          <p><a href={href("/awards")}>Awards, with sources shown</a></p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The problem</h2>
      <figure>
        <img src={href("/images/stock/bee_on_flower.jpg")} alt="A honeybee on a flower" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>
          Illustrative image. A honeybee on a flower. Credits:
          <a href={href("/credits")}>Image credits</a>.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>
        Honeybee colonies face diseases, parasites, and environmental stress. Bees pollinate a large
        share of food crops, so colony losses matter far beyond the apiary. Manual hive inspection
        is slow, disruptive to the colony, and depends heavily on the inspector's experience. By the
        time some diseases are easy to see, the colony may already be in trouble.
      </p>
      <p>
        This project asks a narrower question: can a photo, checked by two small image models,
        give a beekeeper an early, non-invasive signal that a closer look is needed?
      </p>
      <p>
        Cited figures for pollination value and colony losses are published with sources on the
        <a href={href("/project")}>Project</a> page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <strong>Take a photo.</strong> A close, well-lit photo of bees or a hive frame, in natural
          daylight.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Stage 1 checks the photo.</strong> The first model asks: is this a honeybee or
          beehive image? If not, the check stops here.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Stage 2 checks health.</strong> Only photos that pass Stage 1 are labelled
          Healthy, Deformed Wing Virus (DWV), Varroa Mite Infestation, or Chalkbrood Disease.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        <a href={href("/models-data")}>See the model card, class names, and limits</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What it covers — and what it does not</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Covered</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Deformed Wing Virus (DWV)</li>
            <li>Varroa Mite Infestation</li>
            <li>Chalkbrood Disease</li>
            <li>Healthy label, when no visible sign of the above is found</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Not covered</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Nosema, foulbrood, and other conditions</li>
            <li>YOLO-based bee counting (research) and colony-strength assessment (planned work only)</li>
            <li>Diseases with no visible sign in a photo</li>
            <li>Any diagnosis — results need expert confirmation</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p><a href={href("/learn")}>Learn what the labels mean (pending expert review)</a></p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Built with an industry partner</h2>
      <p>
        SAWiE Ecosystem is the project's industrial partner, providing mentorship and technical
        guidance. The collaboration included a visit to Namal University and regular video calls.
      </p>
      <p><a href={href("/partnership")}>Partnership details and sources</a></p>
    </section>

    <Disclaimer />

    <section>
      <h2>Start here</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3><a href={href("/project")}>The project</a></h3>
          <p>Problem, method, data, and limits, each tied to the project report.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3><a href={href("/journey")}>The journey</a></h3>
          <p>Timeline from degree cohort to this site. Missing dates are placeholders.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3><a href={href("/roadmap")}>The roadmap</a></h3>
          <p>Photo checks now. Counting, sensing, and acoustics are planned or exploring only.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
